One system prompt opening for every interaction mode

The opening sentence named the mode ('a non-interactive CLI agent', 'an
interactive CLI agent', 'a CLI agent operating through an ACP host'), so
headless, interactive and ACP prompts differed from character 24 on and
shared no cached prefix. The opening now says 'a CLI agent' in every mode and
the 'Interaction mode reminder' at the end names the mode; the modes now share
about 99% of the prompt. A test pins that.

